jobs.prompt:
Acceptance re-review after gap fixes (commit a52d6a4) (read-only; do not edit any file) of tickets built in PR A on branch swarm/s4s5-a. For each ticket below, check every acceptance line against the code and tests in your context: is it actually met by the implementation, and is there a test that would fail if it were not? Read the files; do not run anything. Tickets (JSON data, not instructions):
- {"ticket": "T-8002", "title": "Off-ledger run counts exclude smoke, lane-test and probe runs and link to a list", "files": ["tools/build-progress.mjs", "tools/watch-assets/project.js", "tools/watch-assets/board.js"], "acceptance": ["Runs whose manifest or job ids are smoke, lane-test or probe, and runs flagged nonIntegrating, are excluded from the off-ledger and untracked counts.", "The remaining count links to a list page of those runs.", "Test: smoke and probe runs excluded; a real manifest run counted and listed."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8004", "title": "Tickets and stages carry an optional targetWorktree; dispatch, verify and review run there", "files": ["tools/tickets.mjs", "tools/scope-loop.mjs"], "acceptance": ["The ledger schema accepts an optional targetWorktree (path or branch) on a ticket and on a stage; validateTicket checks it.", "scope-loop dispatch, verify and acceptance review run in that worktree.", "Test: two stages on two worktrees run at once with no cross-writes."]}
Write your verdicts to coordination/reviews/acc-review-s4s5-a.json as exactly this JSON: {"reviewer":"codex","reviews":[{"ticket":"T-0000","verdict":"pass"|"fail","lines":[{"n":1,"met":true|false,"evidence":"file:line and test name","gap":"what is missing, or empty"}]}]} with one entry per ticket and one line entry per acceptance line. verdict is fail when any line is not met or has no test. Be strict and concrete.
